WEBVTT

00:01:34.610 --> 00:01:36.980
Here’s your usual drug.

00:01:39.950 --> 00:01:41.080
Your money.

00:01:46.130 --> 00:01:48.310
That’s quite generous, my kind sir.

00:01:48.740 --> 00:01:51.600
I know many “bad” patients,

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:54.780
but none of them are as active as you.

00:01:54.780 --> 00:01:56.310
Seems like your business is doing well.

00:01:57.190 --> 00:01:58.620
Don’t tell anyone else or be nosy.

00:01:58.880 --> 00:02:02.760
That goes without saying, doesn’t it?

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:08.080
There.

00:02:10.490 --> 00:02:12.670
T-Thank you...

00:02:15.170 --> 00:02:16.620
I can’t hear you.

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:20.630
Don’t be that cold, Ume.

00:02:21.140 --> 00:02:25.700
You don’t have to be nice to someone who isn’t going to join us, Ichi.

00:02:26.760 --> 00:02:27.550
Eat up.

00:02:28.220 --> 00:02:30.540
You’re such a good Samaritan.

00:02:30.540 --> 00:02:32.250
I’m at a loss for words.

00:02:32.250 --> 00:02:33.560
I can hear you.

00:02:44.990 --> 00:02:48.300
He leaves when the tavern starts to become crowded.

00:02:55.710 --> 00:02:57.950
Where are you going?

00:02:58.680 --> 00:03:00.640
I’m just going back home.

00:03:01.230 --> 00:03:03.010
Where do you live?

00:03:03.010 --> 00:03:07.090
If you need me, just go to Ume’s tavern.

00:03:07.090 --> 00:03:09.990
Uh... I was just trying to strike up a conversation.

00:03:14.070 --> 00:03:18.200
I don’t know anything about him...

00:03:19.080 --> 00:03:20.200
Katsuraya.

00:03:21.490 --> 00:03:25.290
It’s a place that’s in the red-light district of Fukagawa.

00:03:25.290 --> 00:03:26.670
I’m usually there.

00:03:26.670 --> 00:03:27.750
Why do you live there?

00:03:27.750 --> 00:03:28.770
Because it’s my home.

00:03:29.290 --> 00:03:31.610
Please stop teasing me.

00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:35.500
’Night.

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:52.970
Where did you go, Ichi-san?

00:03:52.970 --> 00:03:55.720
You should stop by and have some fun with us once in a while.

00:03:55.720 --> 00:03:58.550
Lately, you’ve been taking pretty long strolls.

00:03:58.550 --> 00:04:00.830
You went to see another girl, didn’t you?

00:04:02.700 --> 00:04:03.830
Sir.

00:04:04.820 --> 00:04:07.250
Oh, my. You don’t look familiar.

00:04:07.250 --> 00:04:09.030
Uh... Well...

00:04:09.030 --> 00:04:11.010
Oh, my. How cute!

00:04:11.440 --> 00:04:14.080
Hm... That guy over there...

00:04:14.080 --> 00:04:15.790
You mean Ichi-san?

00:04:15.790 --> 00:04:17.790
He’s the bodyguard for Katsuraya.

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:19.010
Bodyguard?

00:04:19.370 --> 00:04:21.760
Even though he isn’t carrying swords?

00:04:21.760 --> 00:04:23.760
Ostensibly, he’s a freeloader.

00:04:23.760 --> 00:04:25.930
Anyway, he’s a hottie.

00:04:25.930 --> 00:04:31.830
I heard the girls from Katsuraya frantically sneak into his room instead of getting customers.

00:04:33.120 --> 00:04:35.440
I want him to make love to me, too!

00:04:39.590 --> 00:04:41.210
I really don’t get him.

00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:43.690
He looks quite skilled,

00:04:44.070 --> 00:04:46.080
and his words leave a strong impression as well.

00:04:46.550 --> 00:04:48.420
Just who is he?

00:05:07.600 --> 00:05:08.750
Oh?

00:05:08.750 --> 00:05:12.100
So, you stopped being particular about the bodyguard job?

00:05:12.550 --> 00:05:15.610
I’m glad you came to your senses, Akitsu-sama.

00:05:15.610 --> 00:05:19.060
I have more than enough jobs for day laborers.

00:05:29.090 --> 00:05:31.050
How about putting more power into it?

00:05:31.050 --> 00:05:32.090
Move.

00:05:32.940 --> 00:05:34.900
It’ll be much faster if I do it.

00:05:41.640 --> 00:05:42.380
Masa.

00:05:46.970 --> 00:05:51.400
If you get hungry, you can always go to Ume’s tavern.

00:05:52.250 --> 00:05:52.770
But...

00:05:53.540 --> 00:05:56.430
I’ll talk to him.

00:05:56.980 --> 00:05:58.070
Don’t worry.

00:06:09.420 --> 00:06:12.780
If you can’t even do a heavy labor job,

00:06:12.780 --> 00:06:14.780
how are you going to get money for food?

00:06:14.780 --> 00:06:16.450
Uh... Well...

00:06:16.840 --> 00:06:19.000
Come on. Join us already!

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:20.910
But...

00:06:24.430 --> 00:06:28.040
Ume, you spilled the miso soup.

00:06:28.040 --> 00:06:29.660
Give him a new one.

00:06:31.280 --> 00:06:33.240
Okinu, give him another bowl of soup.

00:06:33.760 --> 00:06:35.430
What? Ah, sure.

00:06:38.150 --> 00:06:40.490
Sorry about that.

00:06:41.190 --> 00:06:43.130
That’s how he is.

00:06:46.960 --> 00:06:49.490
Ah! Welcome, Matsu-san.

00:06:50.070 --> 00:06:51.610
Hey, Matsu!

00:06:51.610 --> 00:06:53.470
This place is pretty crowded tonight.

00:06:53.470 --> 00:06:55.080
Come and have a seat.

00:06:57.100 --> 00:06:59.900
Ume looks so intimidating.

00:06:59.900 --> 00:07:03.660
That’s why only a few regulars come here.

00:07:05.960 --> 00:07:08.210
Matsu is a regular, too.

00:07:08.210 --> 00:07:09.310
Really?

00:07:10.130 --> 00:07:13.410
Damn that Ichi. There’s a limit to being nice.

00:07:13.410 --> 00:07:17.760
We take care of this penniless ronin, but don’t even get anything in return.

00:07:18.550 --> 00:07:19.900
That isn’t even funny.

00:07:20.150 --> 00:07:25.790
Dad, the ladies will hate you if you talk badly about Ichi-san.

00:07:26.690 --> 00:07:28.850
He’s like a celebrity.

00:07:28.850 --> 00:07:31.110
Right, Otake-san?

00:07:31.110 --> 00:07:33.600
He’s handsome.

00:07:36.900 --> 00:07:37.890
Ronin,

00:07:39.420 --> 00:07:41.420
I’m letting you eat for free.

00:07:42.480 --> 00:07:44.290
So, you will help me with the shopping tomorrow.

00:07:46.250 --> 00:07:48.270
S-Sure...

00:08:01.270 --> 00:08:05.080
So... Is it far away?

00:08:27.640 --> 00:08:30.010
What kind of a guy is it this time?

00:08:32.800 --> 00:08:35.970
Just the ordinary brat of a shogun’s vassal.

00:08:49.630 --> 00:08:51.640
Get your act together, for crying out loud.

00:08:54.380 --> 00:08:56.230
We gave him a sleeping pill and stuffed his ears,

00:08:56.230 --> 00:09:01.710
but, as a precaution, we gagged him while we were traveling outside. That’s an ironclad rule.

00:09:01.710 --> 00:09:06.690
I helped you without even noticing what you were doing.

00:09:06.690 --> 00:09:09.550
I told you that you were going to help me with the shopping.

00:09:10.580 --> 00:09:15.250
He isn’t a new member?

00:09:15.250 --> 00:09:18.020
Well, we can almost call him a member.

00:09:18.720 --> 00:09:22.600
Ichi is being nice to you because he expects you to join.

00:09:23.210 --> 00:09:24.760
That’s not...

00:09:24.760 --> 00:09:26.430
That’s not kindness.

00:09:27.120 --> 00:09:30.060
He’s determined to get you to join us.

00:09:32.400 --> 00:09:37.440
You’re terribly mistaken if you think that Yaichi is a nice guy.

00:09:37.440 --> 00:09:40.190
He’s different from someone you’d call kind.

00:09:45.900 --> 00:09:51.100
So, when will he show up here?

00:09:51.820 --> 00:09:55.600
I’ve told him to come here many times, but he doesn’t seem to be interested.

00:09:56.130 --> 00:09:57.770
I’ll drag him here next time.

00:10:08.770 --> 00:10:12.420
I’ve known Ume for a long time.

00:10:13.830 --> 00:10:16.670
I started helping him.

00:10:16.670 --> 00:10:19.710
Well, all I do is take care of the hostages for a few days.

00:10:21.320 --> 00:10:25.850
Anyway, you seem to be a nice guy.

00:10:27.130 --> 00:10:30.100
I guess you aren’t cut out for this job.

00:10:30.560 --> 00:10:33.060
If you don’t want to be involved in all this,

00:10:33.480 --> 00:10:36.080
just get away before it’s too late.

00:10:43.940 --> 00:10:47.000
Just to make this clear in case you’re going to join us:

00:10:47.000 --> 00:10:49.550
If you lay a finger on Otake, you’re dead.

00:10:49.550 --> 00:10:53.690
S-Shouldn’t you say that to Yaichi-dono?

00:10:53.690 --> 00:10:54.550
To Ichi?

00:10:54.960 --> 00:10:58.490
I assumed you hated him because of that.

00:10:58.970 --> 00:11:00.490
I don’t hate him.

00:11:01.090 --> 00:11:03.570
But I don’t trust him either.

00:11:03.570 --> 00:11:05.660
I can’t really figure him out.

00:11:06.520 --> 00:11:10.370
Shouldn’t comrades trust each other?

00:11:11.410 --> 00:11:13.730
He’s a smart guy.

00:11:13.730 --> 00:11:18.170
I don’t trust him, but I have confidence in him.

00:11:27.410 --> 00:11:28.890
However...

00:11:30.900 --> 00:11:34.390
Shoot, it’s empty.

00:11:34.700 --> 00:11:35.420
Here.

00:11:35.420 --> 00:11:37.810
Thanks, Okinu-chan.

00:11:38.870 --> 00:11:42.070
Otake-san, make that the last one for tonight.

00:11:42.070 --> 00:11:42.860
Ume.

00:11:43.330 --> 00:11:44.570
Fill me up, too.

00:11:45.680 --> 00:11:46.780
Please.

00:11:50.730 --> 00:11:56.850
So... I’m in the middle of their circle now.

00:12:23.330 --> 00:12:26.920
I had so much fun on the boat today, Masa. Thanks.

00:12:27.390 --> 00:12:29.580
How about a drink?

00:12:29.580 --> 00:12:33.470
Uh... I-I’m a lightweight when it comes to drinking.

00:12:33.930 --> 00:12:36.160
You don’t want to be with me?

00:12:36.160 --> 00:12:37.550
Hey, ronin!

00:12:37.550 --> 00:12:38.930
Y-Yes?

00:12:39.180 --> 00:12:41.500
Help me in the kitchen.

00:12:41.500 --> 00:12:45.480
Oh, boy! He’s got you helping him out, huh?

00:12:55.290 --> 00:12:56.660
Yaichi-dono.

00:12:57.140 --> 00:12:59.630
A samurai preparing pickles, huh?

00:13:02.050 --> 00:13:04.320
Ume, I’m leaving it here.

00:13:08.150 --> 00:13:13.420
Is that the ransom for the guy we kidnapped yesterday?

00:13:14.010 --> 00:13:17.530
You’re sharp.

00:13:21.970 --> 00:13:24.900
I just came back from picking up the money.

00:13:27.550 --> 00:13:33.120
I guess they’re not taking any risks, despite being kidnappers.

00:13:42.150 --> 00:13:43.760
S-Sorry!

00:13:44.900 --> 00:13:46.500
What the hell did you do?

00:13:46.500 --> 00:13:49.140
It’s all because you wandered in without saying a word.

00:13:49.140 --> 00:13:52.630
Sheesh, such a waste.

00:13:52.630 --> 00:13:55.180
Matsu, this seat is free.

00:13:57.410 --> 00:14:01.190
He and my dad don’t get along.

00:14:01.190 --> 00:14:03.880
Is he here because of Otake-san?

00:14:03.880 --> 00:14:05.120
No idea.

00:14:07.640 --> 00:14:12.280
So, the government doesn’t know about the Five Leaves?

00:14:12.280 --> 00:14:14.720
Well, we know who to threaten and who to avoid.

00:14:14.720 --> 00:14:20.730
By the time they find out about us, we’ll have left Edo already.

00:14:20.730 --> 00:14:23.230
Ichi-san is late, isn’t he?

00:14:23.230 --> 00:14:24.830
What’s special about tonight?

00:14:25.580 --> 00:14:27.290
We’re splitting the money.

00:14:27.290 --> 00:14:28.010
The money?

00:14:28.640 --> 00:14:31.880
I’ll take my leave then.

00:14:32.880 --> 00:14:35.170
Don’t you need money?

00:14:35.170 --> 00:14:38.330
But I didn’t do anything.

00:14:38.330 --> 00:14:42.290
Well, I didn’t do anything this time either.

00:14:42.930 --> 00:14:44.800
Except pick up some maple leaves.

00:14:45.380 --> 00:14:46.480
Maple leaves?

00:14:48.350 --> 00:14:52.450
We put one in a letter and then send it to the victim’s family.

00:14:53.830 --> 00:14:56.690
Along with the name “Five Leaves.”

00:15:06.470 --> 00:15:07.530
Where’s Masa?

00:15:07.530 --> 00:15:09.000
He went home.

00:15:12.670 --> 00:15:15.260
Maybe I should take him out again tomorrow.

00:15:16.000 --> 00:15:17.630
Don’t get too involved with him.

00:15:18.230 --> 00:15:22.090
But you seem to like him.

00:15:24.230 --> 00:15:26.790
Look, a leaf with five lobes.

00:15:26.790 --> 00:15:28.600
This is the emblem of the Five Leaves.

00:15:28.600 --> 00:15:31.330
I just need to pick them, right?

00:15:38.330 --> 00:15:41.940
If you join us, we’ll really become five leaves.

00:15:44.190 --> 00:15:49.080
Otake-dono, Yaichi-dono, Ume-dono and the old man.

00:15:49.080 --> 00:15:51.990
They’ll be complete when I join them.

00:15:51.990 --> 00:15:53.470
I’ll buy some dumplings.

00:15:54.460 --> 00:15:56.060
You keep picking up the leaves.

00:15:58.950 --> 00:16:00.660
I’m being dragged around by her...

00:16:01.140 --> 00:16:03.610
So cold...

00:16:09.340 --> 00:16:12.430
I better start wearing my padded kimono.

00:16:15.440 --> 00:16:18.820
A samurai picking up fallen leaves?

00:16:20.380 --> 00:16:22.290
Well, you don’t see that everyday.

00:16:22.990 --> 00:16:25.060
Did a woman ask you to do that?

00:16:26.850 --> 00:16:28.080
Yes.

00:16:29.330 --> 00:16:32.320
Are you really a samurai?

00:16:35.480 --> 00:16:38.020
Y-Yes, I am!

00:16:49.080 --> 00:16:50.620
You’re pretty funny.

00:16:51.990 --> 00:16:56.360
Just watching you pick up the leaves is funny.

00:16:58.080 --> 00:16:58.960
There you go.

00:17:07.240 --> 00:17:09.630
We don’t need leaves with seven lobes.

00:17:20.270 --> 00:17:21.690
Well, if it isn’t Matsu.

00:17:23.740 --> 00:17:25.120
Are you delivering the tobacco pipes?

00:17:25.590 --> 00:17:27.120
I’m returning that.

00:17:28.770 --> 00:17:29.920
Tobacco pipes?

00:17:30.450 --> 00:17:32.640
He makes ornaments.

00:17:33.520 --> 00:17:34.640
Here.

00:17:35.910 --> 00:17:38.290
The one I promised you.

00:17:38.730 --> 00:17:40.290
A hairpin?

00:17:40.290 --> 00:17:41.650
You made this for me?

00:17:42.150 --> 00:17:43.650
It’s lovely.

00:17:43.650 --> 00:17:44.880
Thank you, Matsu!

00:17:45.670 --> 00:17:48.280
He isn’t even looking at me.

00:17:48.280 --> 00:17:51.480
Is he ignoring me?

00:17:52.700 --> 00:17:53.620
What?!

00:17:54.200 --> 00:17:56.910
Matsu gave Otake a hairpin?!

00:17:56.910 --> 00:17:57.830
Yes.

00:17:57.830 --> 00:18:01.590
Damn him. He finally did it!

00:18:08.000 --> 00:18:09.590
Here, this is your share.

00:18:10.410 --> 00:18:12.180
W-Well...

00:18:12.180 --> 00:18:14.960
You didn’t do anything this time, so your share is one ryo.

00:18:14.960 --> 00:18:16.630
Use it however you want.

00:18:17.570 --> 00:18:18.230
Um...

00:18:18.230 --> 00:18:20.550
By the way, you can pay off your debt to me.

00:18:24.170 --> 00:18:28.930
Do you see me as a member?

00:18:29.470 --> 00:18:30.370
I’m not really sure.

00:18:33.820 --> 00:18:36.920
You’re taking care of the pickles here.

00:18:38.100 --> 00:18:40.820
However, you do know our identities as well.

00:18:41.720 --> 00:18:44.140
Just take it as hush money.

00:18:44.450 --> 00:18:47.180
Don’t worry about it. Just take it.

00:18:47.180 --> 00:18:53.130
Well, if you don’t come here, you won’t have any worries.

00:18:59.530 --> 00:19:01.960
Do you like this place?

00:19:03.560 --> 00:19:05.050
Yes.

00:19:05.660 --> 00:19:10.930
I’ve never had a place in Edo where I could socialize.

00:19:10.930 --> 00:19:13.380
And there’s my personality issue, too.

00:19:14.040 --> 00:19:18.460
I’ve never had any friends, even when I worked at my fiefdom.

00:19:18.460 --> 00:19:20.080
I’m so sorry to hear that!

00:19:20.080 --> 00:19:23.280
That must’ve been so lonely, right, Samurai?

00:19:23.280 --> 00:19:25.080
S-Sorry?

00:19:25.080 --> 00:19:28.550
No, I shouldn’t call you that.

00:19:30.210 --> 00:19:32.920
You’re already one of us.

00:19:32.920 --> 00:19:35.920
Please continue coming here, Masa-san.

00:19:35.920 --> 00:19:41.080
O-Okay, I will.

00:19:42.580 --> 00:19:44.390
All right, let’s drink!

00:19:44.390 --> 00:19:45.670
Let the drinks come!

00:19:45.670 --> 00:19:46.760
Right away.

00:20:06.400 --> 00:20:08.900
How was it, Matsu?

00:20:09.760 --> 00:20:12.820
They didn’t seem to be eager to report to the government officers.

00:20:13.860 --> 00:20:15.600
What about the hostage we returned?

00:20:15.600 --> 00:20:17.600
He was resting at home.

00:20:18.100 --> 00:20:20.490
I’ll continue observing them.

00:20:23.460 --> 00:20:27.450
Matsu, he’s gonna join us.

00:20:27.450 --> 00:20:28.750
That ronin?

00:20:29.200 --> 00:20:32.560
Even without me pushing, he continues to get more involved.

00:20:33.110 --> 00:20:34.660
He’s an interesting man.

00:20:35.240 --> 00:20:36.820
That’s not like you.

00:20:37.630 --> 00:20:41.560
I don’t want him to join because of his skill alone.

00:20:41.560 --> 00:20:43.400
I just don’t get bored of watching him.

00:20:44.350 --> 00:20:48.060
I want to observe him a bit longer to see what kind of person he is.

00:20:48.670 --> 00:20:50.390
What kind of person?

00:20:51.110 --> 00:20:55.620
I know that’s not like me.

00:21:09.050 --> 00:21:16.250
I’ve got a feeling that something was hidden

00:21:16.250 --> 00:21:25.540
in the words you once told me. Those words cross my mind again and again.

00:21:25.540 --> 00:21:33.960
Yet your voice always sounds the same as before.

00:21:33.960 --> 00:21:41.010
Every time I breathe, I wanna hold you in my arms

00:21:41.410 --> 00:21:49.940
Every words you whispered makes my heart beat up and high

00:21:50.780 --> 00:21:58.020
Every time I breathe, I just wanna hold you in my arms again

00:21:59.140 --> 00:22:06.840
Every words you whispered makes my heart beat up and high

00:22:07.500 --> 00:22:15.080
Every day I need you  All the time I'll be there for you

00:22:15.810 --> 00:22:24.190
Every words you whispered makes my heart beat up and high

00:22:30.450 --> 00:22:33.290
Next time on House of Five Leaves:

00:22:33.790 --> 00:22:35.210
Umezou here.

00:22:35.210 --> 00:22:37.240
You have to deal with various things if you’re close to your customers.

00:22:37.840 --> 00:22:41.250
Like a novice ronin coming to eat for free.

00:22:41.850 --> 00:22:46.040
But, you know, I’m a bashful guy, so I can’t even complain.

00:22:46.250 --> 00:22:48.050
Well then, the next episode’s title is:

00:22:48.050 --> 00:22:49.930
“Getting Involved Steadily.”
